{
  "$comment": "The retired-forms ledger (S482). Ruling: scrml-support/user-voice-scrml.md S482 \"⭐ RULED — every retirement / deprecation PR adds a retired-forms ledger row and migrates\" — \"every PR that retires or deprecates a syntax form must do both: 1. add a row to the retired-forms ledger (`compiler/retired-forms.json`): the old form, the new form, its tier, the error or warning code, and the ruling citation; 2. migrate the SPEC examples, or for a deprecated form, record the starting count, which then only goes down.\" HARD rows fail scripts/retired-forms-lint.ts outside labelled negatives, allow markers and the dated `pending` debt in scripts/retired-forms-baseline.json; SOFT rows ratchet per (row, file). `legacyMarker` rows feed scripts/bootstrap-conformance.ts LEGACY_MARKERS (in `order`). A `detector` is a regex over comment- and string-stripped scrml (per line; flag `m` = over the whole text) or a builtin of the lint; null = not detectable from text (the compiler enforces it).",
